    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Energy Against Onsager [S+N]\n\nAway from $T_c$ the correlation length is a few lattice spacings, so the $24 \\times 24$ lattice should reproduce the infinite-lattice energy to within the statistical error. The table compares the two at the temperatures furthest from $T_c$.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "u_f(t) := float(subst(T = t, u_ons))$\nT_grid : sublist(makelist(1.2 + 0.01*i, i, 0, 240), lambda([t], abs(t - Tc_f) > 1.0e-4))$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"black\", name=\"Onsager\", lines(T_grid, map(u_f, T_grid)),\n  color=\"darkorange\", marker_size=7, name=\"L = 12\", points(Ts, column(res12, 3)),\n  color=\"steelblue\", name=\"L = 24\", points(Ts, column(res24, 3)),\n  title=\"Energy per Spin\", xlabel=\"T\", ylabel=\"<E>/N\", showlegend=true)$\n\nprintf(true, \"    T   MC L=24    Onsager    difference~%\")$\nfor k in [1, 2, 3, 14, 15] do\n  printf(true, \"~5,2f   ~7,4f    ~7,4f    ~8,4f~%\", Ts[k], res24[k][3], u_f(Ts[k]),\n         res24[k][3] - u_f(Ts[k]))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 15,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
