    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Heat Capacity [S+N]\n\nThe exact heat capacity diverges logarithmically at $T_c$. A finite lattice gives a finite peak instead, and the peak sits slightly above $T_c$. Both effects shrink as $L$ grows.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "c_f(t) := float(subst(T = t, c_ons))$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"black\", name=\"Onsager\", lines(T_grid, map(c_f, T_grid)),\n  color=\"darkorange\", marker_size=7, name=\"L = 12\", points(Ts, column(res12, 4)),\n  color=\"steelblue\", name=\"L = 24\", points(Ts, column(res24, 4)),\n  title=\"Heat Capacity per Spin\", xlabel=\"T\", ylabel=\"c\", yrange=[0, 3.5],\n  showlegend=true)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 16,
